# Emrakul, the Exigent Doom's activated ability has one target, the land. Bot1 activates it on Bot2's turn, exiling
# Emrakul as the cost, and Bot2 answers with Strip Mine on that Island. With its only target gone the ability does not
# resolve at all (CR 608.2b), so it gives no permission either: Emrakul stays in exile and, with ten mana open on Bot1's
# next turn, cannot be cast from there, while the Black Lotus that could pay for it is offered.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Emrakul, the Exigent Doom
Black Lotus x4
Swamp
Swamp x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Strip Mine
Swamp x14

